1
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:06,920
Popcorn sales are slow today.
It's pretty chill.

2
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:08,090
Niimi-san.

3
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:10,050
I wish every day was like this.

4
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:13,880
Ah, I'll take over.
You go take a break.

5
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:15,840
Thanks.
I'll go take my break then.

6
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:18,310
Oh, right.

7
00:00:18,390 --> 00:00:19,390
What is it?

8
00:00:21,270 --> 00:00:22,530
Your friend is here.

9
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:24,880
Huh?

10
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:35,550
Chiharu.

11
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:37,879
What are you doing here?

12
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:38,939
You could've at least said hi.

13
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:39,940
Sorry, sorry.

14
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,180
I was shopping and thought I'd
drop by to see if you were here.

15
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:44,000
You looked busy, so I
didn't call out to you.

16
00:00:45,940 --> 00:00:50,730
Here. I bought a different
style from the one I gave you.

17
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:52,360
Because I wanted one for myself too.

18
00:00:52,440 --> 00:00:54,320
"The Jet-Black Hawk" is pretty good, though.

19
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:56,700
By the way, do you want to
catch a movie before you go?

20
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:59,000
Since you're here, consider
it my birthday present to you.

21
00:00:59,350 --> 00:01:02,390
Thanks.
But I want to watch a movie with you.

22
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:05,440
And as for my birthday, I want to
save the celebration for the weekend.

23
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:07,600
I see.

24
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:10,359
Well, good luck with work.

25
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:12,620
Yeah, see you this weekend.

26
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:14,360
- See ya.
- Yeah.

27
00:01:25,870 --> 00:01:27,720
What?
Did he leave?

28
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:30,040
He said he was just dropping by.

29
00:01:30,130 --> 00:01:32,650
Oh, to see you, Toda-kun?

30
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:37,059
Well... I'm not sure if
I should say yes or no.

31
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:39,339
Anyway, no.
I mean, it's not like that.

32
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:41,660
Or rather...
I don't really know myself.

33
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:43,300
I'm going to take my break now.

34
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:55,500
(Chiharu's Birthday)

35
00:02:06,420 --> 00:02:11,000
Since then, we've both been busy with college and
work, so we haven't really been able to see each other.

36
00:02:26,260 --> 00:02:28,890
There should be some
progress next time, right?

37
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:31,960
Next time for what?

38
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,660
Ah, sorry.

39
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:36,119
It's nothing, really.

40
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:37,240
Why are you so flustered?

41
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:39,990
- No, I'm not flustered.
- What's wrong with you?

42
00:02:40,020 --> 00:02:41,209
Is something bothering you?

43
00:02:41,210 --> 00:02:42,759
No, nothing's bothering me.

44
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:43,796
Come on.
You obviously have something on your mind.

45
00:02:43,820 --> 00:02:44,580
You even tripped just now.

46
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:45,959
No, no, it's just...

47
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:47,370
It's okay, tell me about it.

48
00:02:47,620 --> 00:02:48,410
Can I?

49
00:02:48,411 --> 00:02:50,039
Yeah, I am older than you, after all.

50
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:52,760
Saito-san is definitely reliable, but...

51
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:55,839
Well, as a person...

52
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:57,899
That look on your face is basically
a roundabout way of saying I'm unreliable.

53
00:02:57,900 --> 00:02:59,300
That's not what I meant.

54
00:02:59,820 --> 00:03:01,579
- Let me help.
- Trust...

55
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:03,239
- I'll take that.
- Trust...

56
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:05,920
Trust...

57
00:03:06,780 --> 00:03:08,439
I do trust you.
I really do.

58
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:10,350
Really? Then what is it?

59
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:45,500
"My Summer Of You" (Episode 9)

60
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:47,739
- That was pretty fast.
- Surprisingly fast.

61
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:49,769
Sorry for the wait.
Here are your lemon sours.

62
00:04:49,770 --> 00:04:50,770
Thank you.

63
00:04:51,860 --> 00:04:56,059
Now that we're all set,
happy birthday.

64
00:04:56,060 --> 00:04:57,840
Cheers.

65
00:05:05,300 --> 00:05:06,300
How is it?

66
00:05:06,730 --> 00:05:08,559
Yeah, it's pretty good.

67
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:09,939
Right?
It goes down smooth.

68
00:05:09,940 --> 00:05:10,959
Yeah.

69
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:12,719
Ah, let me have a sip of yours too.

70
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:14,280
Huh? They're the exact same drink.

71
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:16,320
Are you drunk already?

72
00:05:16,350 --> 00:05:17,379
No, I'm not.

73
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:18,520
I just made a mistake.

74
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:21,729
Besides, I figure
I have a super high tolerance for alcohol.

75
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:23,619
You're totally jinxing yourself right now.

76
00:05:23,620 --> 00:05:24,900
I am not.

77
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:30,450
So,
how does it feel to be twenty?

78
00:05:32,410 --> 00:05:34,080
It doesn't feel like anything's changed.

79
00:05:34,910 --> 00:05:35,680
Ah.

80
00:05:35,750 --> 00:05:37,290
I'm glad I caught up to you.

81
00:05:38,980 --> 00:05:39,980
Oh, right.

82
00:05:41,090 --> 00:05:42,810
My time as the older one was way too short.

83
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:45,760
Well then.

84
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:49,580
Before Chiharu gets drunk.

85
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:52,359
Here, your birthday present.

86
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:53,770
Whoa, really?

87
00:05:54,180 --> 00:05:55,669
Thanks.
Can I open it?

88
00:05:55,670 --> 00:05:56,670
Of course.

89
00:05:58,440 --> 00:05:59,440
Huh?

90
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:02,230
Seriously?
I'm so happy right now.

91
00:06:02,940 --> 00:06:04,980
I thought we could use
them together at your place.

92
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:07,529
I'll make you coffee with this next time.

93
00:06:07,530 --> 00:06:08,530
Yeah.

94
00:06:12,110 --> 00:06:14,070
By the way, this sour really
does go down smooth.

95
00:06:15,070 --> 00:06:16,729
Are you sure you should
be drinking it that fast?

96
00:06:16,730 --> 00:06:17,730
It's fine.

97
00:06:17,850 --> 00:06:19,310
It basically tastes like juice.

98
00:06:21,370 --> 00:06:25,129
This one is Wataru's,
and this one is mine?

99
00:06:25,130 --> 00:06:27,309
Excuse me.
Could I get another lemon sour, please?

100
00:06:27,310 --> 00:06:28,530
Sure, coming right up.

101
00:06:29,790 --> 00:06:31,409
Huh? You finished it already?

102
00:06:31,410 --> 00:06:33,510
Well, it's pretty good.

103
00:06:33,650 --> 00:06:34,699
Are you okay?

104
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:35,680
I'm fine.

105
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:38,940
Wataru, we're almost there. Hang in there.

106
00:06:38,970 --> 00:06:40,939
Hmm? We're at your place already?

107
00:06:40,940 --> 00:06:41,940
Yeah.

108
00:06:41,970 --> 00:06:43,050
I'm unlocking the door now.

109
00:06:44,710 --> 00:06:45,710
Let me help.

110
00:06:45,711 --> 00:06:47,030
No need.

111
00:06:47,370 --> 00:06:49,969
I'm going to stay up all night
watching movies until morning.

112
00:06:49,970 --> 00:06:50,970
Okay, okay.

113
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:52,489
I got it, I got it.

114
00:06:52,490 --> 00:06:53,330
Seriously.

115
00:06:53,331 --> 00:06:58,080
Anyway, where were we?

116
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:00,370
We should've just drank at home.

117
00:07:00,750 --> 00:07:01,750
Hmm?

118
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,090
Nothing, never mind.

119
00:07:03,590 --> 00:07:05,300
You were talking about Niimi-san.

120
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:07,089
Right, right, right.

121
00:07:07,090 --> 00:07:08,799
Niimi-san.

122
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:13,070
I told him about how we went
on that pilgrimage together.

123
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:15,240
And he said he wanted
to go check it out too.

124
00:07:16,850 --> 00:07:22,220
Niimi-san is a grad
student and really smart.

125
00:07:23,350 --> 00:07:26,190
He's super easy to talk to.

126
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:31,490
You guys sure are close.

127
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:36,200
What's with that?

128
00:07:36,950 --> 00:07:39,200
Just spit it out if you
have something to say.

129
00:07:39,410 --> 00:07:40,890
No, it's nothing.

130
00:07:42,650 --> 00:07:43,660
What is it?

131
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:45,959
Just say it...

132
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:46,960
Wataru, wait.

133
00:08:01,730 --> 00:08:02,730
Hey.

134
00:08:03,350 --> 00:08:05,440
I wasn't finished talking.

135
00:08:06,650 --> 00:08:08,580
That's what you get for
looking at me like that.

136
00:08:11,470 --> 00:08:12,910
By the way, your face is burning up.

137
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:14,509
That's because I'm drunk...

138
00:08:14,510 --> 00:08:15,510
Hmm?

139
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:17,580
Hey, I am not drunk.

140
00:08:20,450 --> 00:08:22,790
But...

141
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:29,350
Your hands are so cool.
They feel really nice.

142
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:45,450
Wataru, drink some water.

143
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:46,820
I'll go get some.

144
00:08:49,810 --> 00:08:52,750
Wait, Wataru.

145
00:08:53,740 --> 00:08:54,740
Hey.

146
00:08:56,160 --> 00:09:00,040
You wanted to kiss me just now, didn't you?

147
00:09:00,950 --> 00:09:02,120
No, I didn't.

148
00:09:02,290 --> 00:09:03,580
Liar.

149
00:09:04,050 --> 00:09:08,690
It's really frustrating when you tease me
and then just stop halfway.

150
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:10,189
No kissing today.

151
00:09:10,190 --> 00:09:11,210
Why not?

152
00:09:11,590 --> 00:09:12,590
No reason.

153
00:09:12,870 --> 00:09:15,900
You literally said you
wanted to kiss me before.

154
00:09:19,190 --> 00:09:22,220
Because I'm afraid I
won't be able to hold back.

155
00:09:23,310 --> 00:09:24,310
Huh?

156
00:09:25,610 --> 00:09:28,660
It's just a kiss.
You don't have to hold back.

157
00:09:30,020 --> 00:09:32,690
I'm growing up too, you know.

158
00:09:32,810 --> 00:09:34,370
Yeah, but...

159
00:09:39,870 --> 00:09:41,670
There's no way it would
end with just a kiss.

160
00:09:43,030 --> 00:09:44,030
Hmm?

161
00:09:44,710 --> 00:09:47,470
I don't want you getting drunk
and forgetting everything the next day.

162
00:09:47,550 --> 00:09:49,640
Plus, there's another problem before that.

163
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:51,840
What problem?

164
00:09:52,610 --> 00:09:53,970
Wataru, you're sleepy, aren't you?

165
00:09:56,230 --> 00:09:58,320
No, I'm not...

166
00:10:00,070 --> 00:10:01,860
It's your birthday today.

167
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:03,850
I'm not going to sleep yet.

168
00:10:04,850 --> 00:10:07,060
You don't have to force yourself.

169
00:10:11,980 --> 00:10:12,980
Here.

170
00:10:13,630 --> 00:10:14,750
Are you going to sleep here?

171
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:18,360
Yeah...

172
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:28,930
I just suddenly realized.

173
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:31,080
I...

174
00:10:32,390 --> 00:10:34,690
I think I really like your scent.

175
00:10:37,190 --> 00:10:40,210
It makes me feel so safe...

176
00:10:55,940 --> 00:10:57,340
That's not fair.

177
00:11:31,270 --> 00:11:32,400
Chiharu?

178
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:46,918
(Wataru: I have some things to take care of
at the university this morning, so I'm heading

179
00:11:46,942 --> 00:11:50,200
out for a bit. I'll be back after noon. If you
want to head home first, you can use this key.)

180
00:11:52,500 --> 00:11:54,640
Wow, that guy has plans today.

181
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:57,210
Huh, what time is it?

182
00:11:59,340 --> 00:12:01,230
It's already eleven...

183
00:12:01,790 --> 00:12:04,280
How long did I sleep?

184
00:12:07,410 --> 00:12:08,410
Huh?

185
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:10,830
Where did I fall asleep yesterday?

186
00:12:13,990 --> 00:12:16,870
It makes me feel so safe...

187
00:12:18,650 --> 00:12:19,650
Ah, stop, stop, stop.

188
00:12:19,651 --> 00:12:21,131
Let's not think about that right now.

189
00:12:22,130 --> 00:12:24,250
I'll just watch a movie and
wait for him to get back.

190
00:12:25,070 --> 00:12:27,340
Huh, where's the remote?

191
00:12:27,950 --> 00:12:28,950
Where is it?

192
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:30,900
Hmm?

193
00:12:30,950 --> 00:12:32,290
Oh, here it is.

194
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:42,100
(Exchange Program Participant Briefing)

195
00:12:42,170 --> 00:12:43,170
Wow...

196
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:53,730
The requirements are higher than I thought.

197
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:55,950
You'll definitely be fine.

198
00:12:56,060 --> 00:12:58,440
No, if it were just an English test, maybe.

199
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:01,520
But in our department,
they even review our portfolios.

200
00:13:02,230 --> 00:13:03,900
I need to start working on it early.

201
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,980
Hold on, sorry.
Wataru just texted me.

202
00:13:12,410 --> 00:13:13,970
Sorry, I fell asleep again.

203
00:13:14,290 --> 00:13:16,330
I have something to do
later, so I'll head out now.

204
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:18,040
What did he say?

205
00:13:18,930 --> 00:13:22,050
Nothing much. He stayed over at my place
last night and was talking about that.

206
00:13:22,550 --> 00:13:23,550
I see.

207
00:13:26,490 --> 00:13:27,490
By the way, Chiharu.

208
00:13:29,550 --> 00:13:31,920
What are your plans for summer vacation?

209
00:13:32,390 --> 00:13:33,910
Summer vacation?

210
00:13:34,270 --> 00:13:36,580
I haven't decided yet. Why?

211
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:38,860
Oh, nothing.

212
00:13:39,490 --> 00:13:40,710
Let's talk about it next time.

213
00:13:41,190 --> 00:13:42,940
I have an appointment later.

214
00:13:43,490 --> 00:13:44,190
Okay.

215
00:13:44,191 --> 00:13:45,650
See you next time.

216
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:46,990
See you.

217
00:13:57,500 --> 00:13:59,420
(I'm sorry you came all
the way here to see me.)

218
00:14:04,720 --> 00:14:08,010
I didn't do anything stupid
after getting drunk, did I?

219
00:14:18,650 --> 00:14:19,650
Hmm?

220
00:14:21,050 --> 00:14:22,129
You're awake?

221
00:14:22,130 --> 00:14:23,230
You can go back to sleep.

222
00:14:23,270 --> 00:14:24,390
I'm going to clean up a bit.

223
00:14:24,900 --> 00:14:27,569
Hey, where are you going?

224
00:14:27,570 --> 00:14:29,110
Nowhere, just going to clean up.

225
00:14:29,870 --> 00:14:32,160
Come on, I'll help too.

226
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:33,410
No need.

227
00:14:33,450 --> 00:14:34,450
Just keep sleeping.

228
00:14:35,430 --> 00:14:37,790
I won't let you have your way.

229
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:39,040
Why not?

230
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:42,420
Listen to me.

231
00:14:48,130 --> 00:14:50,180
Stay right here.

232
00:14:56,310 --> 00:14:57,520
Got it.

233
00:15:04,510 --> 00:15:05,580
I'll stay here.

234
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:30,000
(I slept all the way until morning.)

235
00:15:41,190 --> 00:15:44,570
- Wataru, I missed you so much.
- You're being too cheesy.

236
00:15:44,770 --> 00:15:46,950
Wait, didn't we just
see each other recently?

237
00:15:46,980 --> 00:15:48,109
Idiot.

238
00:15:48,110 --> 00:15:50,989
I missed you so much I was going crazy.

239
00:15:50,990 --> 00:15:53,070
Coming on too strong will
just make people hate you.

240
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:54,269
What about Hiraoka?

241
00:15:54,270 --> 00:15:55,739
- Is he busy with his club?
- It's alright.

242
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:57,989
I heard you're pretty busy with your
part-time job at the movie theater too.

243
00:15:57,990 --> 00:15:59,370
Yeah.

244
00:15:59,550 --> 00:16:00,660
But it's pretty fun.

245
00:16:01,310 --> 00:16:07,050
Oh, there's a guy with glasses named
Niimi-san. He's super easy to talk to.

246
00:16:07,420 --> 00:16:10,009
Maybe I just get along really
well with guys who wear glasses.

247
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:10,630
Oh.

248
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:11,800
What?

249
00:16:12,380 --> 00:16:14,850
A rival has appeared.

250
00:16:15,550 --> 00:16:18,200
I won't give up the title of Wataru's
favorite glasses guy to anyone else.

251
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:20,030
Who are you even competing with?

252
00:16:22,010 --> 00:16:22,980
Closing in, closing in.
What do you mean, favorite glasses guy?

253
00:16:23,971 --> 00:16:25,291
Isn't there a best glasses award?

254
00:16:25,550 --> 00:16:26,909
For that guy? No?

255
00:16:26,910 --> 00:16:30,030
If you're going to bring something like
that up, get your facts straight first.

256
00:16:31,030 --> 00:16:32,030
Stop dipping it.

257
00:16:32,290 --> 00:16:33,549
- It's fine.
- It's so annoying.

258
00:16:33,550 --> 00:16:35,790
- Okay, sorry.
- Alright, time to study.

259
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:45,330
I didn't expect to still be prepping for exams
with you guys even after getting into college.

260
00:16:46,730 --> 00:16:48,800
Even though we're all in different majors.

261
00:16:49,790 --> 00:16:50,990
It's really a huge help.

262
00:16:51,530 --> 00:16:53,316
It's easy to get distracted
when studying alone.

263
00:16:53,340 --> 00:16:54,820
What's that? Wataru, you're so dirty.

264
00:16:55,220 --> 00:16:57,220
That's just your own dirty mind, Guchi.

265
00:16:57,390 --> 00:16:59,630
Wataru, ever since this guy
started working part-time...

266
00:17:01,140 --> 00:17:02,140
Hmm? Part-time job?

267
00:17:02,270 --> 00:17:03,939
This guy started working at a restaurant.

268
00:17:03,940 --> 00:17:06,660
Seems like things are going pretty well
with a senior coworker there.

269
00:17:07,650 --> 00:17:10,440
Hiraoka, I told you not to
jump ahead on your own.

270
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:12,510
It's just a little bit.

271
00:17:12,550 --> 00:17:13,909
We just get along well, that's all.

272
00:17:13,910 --> 00:17:15,529
Tell me, tell me!

273
00:17:15,530 --> 00:17:16,929
What kind of person are they?

274
00:17:16,930 --> 00:17:19,830
Just leave me out of this.

275
00:17:19,930 --> 00:17:22,226
What about you, Wataru? Are you
working part-time over the summer too?

276
00:17:22,250 --> 00:17:23,160
Yeah.

277
00:17:23,161 --> 00:17:24,569
Aren't you going on a trip or something?

278
00:17:24,570 --> 00:17:26,186
Didn't you go on that trip
with Saeki back in high school?

279
00:17:26,210 --> 00:17:27,290
It was a pilgrimage, right?

280
00:17:28,910 --> 00:17:30,170
Ah...

281
00:17:31,090 --> 00:17:32,210
I don't know.

282
00:17:32,890 --> 00:17:35,220
He seems really busy with work and school.

283
00:17:37,010 --> 00:17:38,510
Oh, you can go with me instead.

284
00:17:38,550 --> 00:17:41,689
Didn't we even have a
sleepover back in middle school?

285
00:17:41,690 --> 00:17:43,429
I told you to stop competing.

286
00:17:43,430 --> 00:17:44,150
Huh?

287
00:17:44,151 --> 00:17:45,329
You're always trying to
compete over everything.

288
00:17:45,330 --> 00:17:46,710
I'm not competing.

289
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:54,600
(Saeki sent a message.)

290
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:58,700
(Do you want to go see a movie later?)

291
00:18:18,550 --> 00:18:20,150
Did I get here too early?

292
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:40,570
Excuse me.

293
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:42,499
Excuse me.

294
00:18:42,500 --> 00:18:46,680
- Yes?
- Could you tell me where the subway is?

295
00:18:46,840 --> 00:18:49,859
Uh, the subway station?

296
00:18:49,860 --> 00:18:50,860
Ah, yes.

297
00:18:51,580 --> 00:18:56,130
Uh, go down those stairs over there.

298
00:18:56,220 --> 00:19:00,550
Head towards the station's West Exit...

299
00:19:01,360 --> 00:19:02,499
Uh...

300
00:19:02,500 --> 00:19:05,000
Station.

301
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:06,100
Hmm...

302
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:09,060
Hmm... West...

303
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:11,839
I'm trying to find the subway,

304
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:12,859
but I'm lost.

305
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:14,230
Even with the map.

306
00:19:16,700 --> 00:19:17,750
I can help.

307
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:19,080
Huh? Chiharu?

308
00:19:20,220 --> 00:19:21,220
Really?

309
00:19:21,450 --> 00:19:24,119
Go down those stairs and walk straight.

310
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:25,580
The subway is there.

311
00:19:25,790 --> 00:19:26,879
OK.

312
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:28,199
Thank you for your help.

313
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:29,200
You are welcome.

314
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:30,520
Bye.

315
00:19:36,260 --> 00:19:37,509
Hmm? What's wrong?

316
00:19:37,510 --> 00:19:38,510
Oh, nothing.

317
00:19:38,670 --> 00:19:41,679
It's just my first time hearing you speak
English. I think it's really impressive.

318
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:43,050
It's nothing, really.

319
00:19:43,300 --> 00:19:45,219
I just know a little bit
because I used to live there.

320
00:19:45,220 --> 00:19:46,399
You call that a little bit?

321
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:47,400
Yeah.

322
00:19:47,430 --> 00:19:50,140
If I want to use it for work,
I'll need to learn a lot more.

323
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:52,560
- Let's go.
- Yeah.

324
00:19:56,800 --> 00:19:59,200
(Exchange Student
Program Information Session)

325
00:20:29,850 --> 00:20:32,140
That was more interesting than I expected.

326
00:20:32,310 --> 00:20:35,519
The subtitles for the jokes were translated
perfectly to fit Japanese culture.

327
00:20:35,520 --> 00:20:36,830
I learned a lot.

328
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:38,960
Yeah.

329
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:40,860
Wataru?

330
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:42,100
Huh?

331
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:43,990
Nothing, nothing. The subtitles, right?

332
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:45,300
You're right.

333
00:20:45,340 --> 00:20:47,060
After all, you're going to be a translator.

334
00:20:47,700 --> 00:20:48,700
Wataru.

335
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:50,080
I'm sorry.

336
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:53,930
Actually, I've been looking for a chance
to tell you this in person.

337
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:57,380
Tell me what?

338
00:20:59,780 --> 00:21:00,810
You know,

339
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:04,480
my favorite thing about Director
Zaizen's films is the dialogue.

340
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:07,610
There are so many seemingly casual lines
that really touch your heart.

341
00:21:09,140 --> 00:21:13,230
Because of that, I started getting
interested in English dialogue too.

342
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:17,580
Translating within constraints
is actually really fascinating.

343
00:21:20,980 --> 00:21:25,280
I hope that one day, I can take words
that will become someone's treasure

344
00:21:25,570 --> 00:21:28,330
and convey them through translation.

345
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:37,080
Just like what you once said to me.

346
00:21:37,710 --> 00:21:40,030
"If you don't like it,
you can just say you don't like it."

347
00:21:40,170 --> 00:21:42,130
"What are your true feelings?"

348
00:21:42,710 --> 00:21:43,710
Huh?

349
00:21:44,680 --> 00:21:48,070
No, no, no. I don't remember
saying anything that profound.

350
00:21:48,350 --> 00:21:50,890
I usually just blurt things out
reflexively.

351
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:53,230
I knew you'd say that.

352
00:21:54,230 --> 00:21:55,230
It's fine.

353
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:57,040
As long as I understand, that's enough.

354
00:22:15,250 --> 00:22:16,250
Am I...

355
00:22:16,600 --> 00:22:18,520
going to hold him back?

356
00:22:18,724 --> 00:22:22,050
[He's looking at search results
for "Translator for Movies"]

357
00:22:29,940 --> 00:22:31,760
After hearing him say that...

358
00:22:32,310 --> 00:22:35,200
how could I possibly ask him if
he's going to study abroad again?

359
00:22:38,300 --> 00:22:41,670
The more I know him, the more I realize
what an incredible catch he is.

360
00:22:42,520 --> 00:22:44,210
So what is it that I want to do?

361
00:22:44,690 --> 00:22:45,750
What about you, Toda-kun?

362
00:22:45,940 --> 00:22:47,530
Do you want to go into filming too?

363
00:22:47,610 --> 00:22:48,450
Huh?

364
00:22:48,540 --> 00:22:50,380
Don't you like movies?

365
00:23:31,990 --> 00:23:33,020
What's wrong?

366
00:23:33,530 --> 00:23:34,530
Hey.

367
00:23:35,800 --> 00:23:36,800
Um...

368
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:39,810
For summer vacation, the
pilgrimage for "Blueprint"...

369
00:23:40,420 --> 00:23:41,500
Do you want to go together?

370
00:24:45,500 --> 00:24:47,876
(Next Episode) Because if I take my eyes off you
for a second, you'll wander off somewhere else.

371
00:24:47,900 --> 00:24:50,239
Don't they say people show their
true colors when they're drunk?

372
00:24:50,240 --> 00:24:52,939
I just haven't been able to
bring myself to ask Wataru out.

373
00:24:52,940 --> 00:24:54,959
I have something I want to tell you.

374
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:55,960
Me too.

375
00:24:57,410 --> 00:24:58,410
We're outside, you know.

376
00:24:58,411 --> 00:24:59,620
It's just a dream anyway.
